Z||000001||Philphine||10-31-2001||08:58 AM||||i used a co. called a to z transport about a year ago cal. to ky.. it went as planned more or less. i've only done something like that once (other time u-hauled it myself) so i can't make any comparision to other companies.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-31-2001||11:05 AM||||I had two Fieros trucked about 700 mile one way from a local firm.  A two day trip out (speed limits)two days back over toll roads.  The cost was a little less than a buck a mile for the experience. ($1400)||||reg||1
Z||000003||NEPTUNE||10-31-2001||12:09 PM||||Be VERY CAREFUL! No govt. agency regulates car haulers. If they damage your car and refuse to pay, you are completely at their mercy. Get references and check them out!<BR>I wish I could recommend someone, but I only hear about the bad ones.  ||||reg||4
Z||000004||CoolBlue87GT||10-31-2001||07:42 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by fierodoug5:<BR>[B]Anyone have a Transport Company they have had good times with?? <P>Yes, I used a company named Dependable Auto Shippers, Inc (DAS)  1(800)626-2505<BR> <A HREF="http://www.dasautoshippers.com/introduction.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dasautoshippers.com/introduction.html</A> <P>I shipped my Fiero from from Maryland to Florida in 98. They were great !<P>They're insured and the car was shipped inside the truck.  It arrived in perfect condition.<P>In their web page, there's a quote page that is kind of neat. Just fill it out, and the computer sends an email back with a free quote.<P>Good luck on your move, hope this helps you out.||||reg||6
